{
  "_doc": ["The canon continent of the Tensura world (Life 2) is Lerfing's map, imported 1:1 as the overworld of world-ttl (design/architecture/lerfing-import.md; map by Lerfing, giant trees by Paulzero). World 0, 0 = Lerfing's 0, 0. canon_map.txt holds one character per chunk of his inner tiles; this file says what each letter is. Lore per region: design/lore/world.md. Every canon place, with its coordinates: design/data/anchors.toml.", "lerfing.inner: the imported inner tiles [x0, z0, x1, z1] (blocks; 1,016 x 784 chunks). lerfing.polygons: one or more polygons per region letter, [[x, z], ...] in world blocks, tried in listed order; tools/lerfing_grid.py gives every land cell the first polygon holding its centre, else the nearest polygon's letter, and regenerates canon_map.txt (run it after an edit, then python tools/gen_map.py).", "Imported chunks are never generated, so inside the inner tiles the climate knobs (temperature, vegetation, erosion, strength), the 'biomes' palettes, replace_peaks and peaks shape nothing: Lerfing's stored biomes rule (WP-L1 repaints the Nether/End ones offline). They stay as documentation and for CanonBiomes' fallback. RegionTitles, /ttlregion, factions and nations read name, colour and banner_*.", "zones (J only): rings by radius from Tempest (owner decision Q4, 19/11/2026): core r 200 +- fade tensura:ancient_forest (20,000 magicule), dark band r 600 +- fade minecraft:dark_forest (2,000), the rest keeps Lerfing's own biome (safe, 500). The offline import repaints the land cells by these rings; /ttlregion and the arrival self-check read them here. centre = tempest in anchors.toml.", "landmarks: named canon places for the map and the data (gen_data.py, gen_map.py); `at` = world [x, z] and must equal the anchors.toml anchor that names it (canon = ...).", "ring: open sea around the land bbox (blocks) before the free, non-canon lands; blend: blocks over which the sea fades into them. The generated ring starts at the edge of the inner tiles (476-696 blocks beyond the land).", "sites: none. They only shaped chunks the generator makes, and no canon build stands on a generated chunk any more; builds are fitted by the placer (survey, fit, repair.js). The key stays so every reader parses the file."],
